@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- OPES O-Car: Quy tắc điều khoản sản phẩm bảo hiểm vật chất xe ô tô
-- (Decision 124/2019/QĐ-TGĐ, amended by the supplementary clauses of Decision 17/2022/QĐ-TGĐ).
-- THE NOUNS: DECLARE and nothing else. Every rule module imports this one.
--
-- Source: ../../source/raw/opes-ocar.txt, the `pdftotext -layout` rendering of
-- opes-ocar.pdf (sha256 c1be5bec...e62e9eca118), retrieved 2026-10-06. A `src:N` comment
-- quotes line N of that file and is generated by tools/vnsrc.py; nothing in Vietnamese
-- here is typed by hand.
--
-- Money is Vietnamese dong (VND), a bare NUMBER. A rate or a share is a NUMBER (70% is 0.7).
-- Membership test for this module: a witness of ordinary competence could testify to the
-- fact, or the certificate, the registration papers, an assessment report or a police
-- record states it. Whether the fact makes a loss payable is a rule, and belongs in the
-- article module that says so.

§ `Nouns for the O-Car rules`

§§ `The parties`

-- src:76 | 1.3. “Bên Mua Bảo Hiểm” là tổ chức, cá nhân giao kết Hợp Đồng Bảo Hiểm với
-- src:77 | Công Ty Bảo Hiểm và đóng Phí Bảo Hiểm. Bên Mua Bảo Hiểm có thể là Người
-- src:78 | Được Bảo Hiểm.
-- src:79 | 1.4. “Người Được Bảo Hiểm” là Chủ Xe có Xe Ô Tô được bảo hiểm theo Hợp Đồng
-- src:80 | Bảo Hiểm vật chất Xe Ô Tô.
-- src:81 | 1.5. “Lái Xe” là người điều khiển Xe Được Bảo Hiểm tại thời điểm xảy ra tổn thất.
-- src:71 | 1.2. “Chủ Xe” là cá nhân, tổ chức sở hữu Xe Ô Tô hoặc cá nhân, tổ chức được chủ
-- src:72 | sở hữu Xe Ô Tô giao chiếm hữu, sử dụng, thuê Xe Ô Tô (theo thỏa thuận thuê
-- src:73 | Xe Ô Tô) hoặc cá nhân, tổ chức là chủ sở hữu thực tế (trường hợp đã mua xe,
-- src:74 | có hợp đồng mua bán Xe Ô Tô hợp pháp) nhưng chưa làm thủ tục đăng ký,
-- src:75 | chưa chuyển đổi tên chủ sở hữu xe theo quy định.
-- src:124 | 1.14. “Công Ty Bảo Hiểm” là Công ty cổ phần bảo hiểm OPES, được thành lập và
-- src:125 | hoạt động theo giấy phép số 79 GP/KDBH ngày 20/03/2018 của Bộ Tài chính.
DECLARE `A party` IS ONE OF
    `the Insurer`         -- Công Ty Bảo Hiểm (1.14)
    `the Policyholder`    -- Bên Mua Bảo Hiểm (1.3)
    `the Insured`         -- Người Được Bảo Hiểm (1.4)
    `the Vehicle Owner`   -- Chủ Xe (1.2)
    `the Driver`          -- Lái Xe (1.5)
    `a data subject`      -- Chủ thể dữ liệu (personal data clause, opening paragraph)

§§ `The acts the rules speak of`

-- The acts that the regulative rules (Articles 3 to 6, 10 and the personal data clause)
-- oblige, permit or forbid. An act is a fact a witness can see done.
DECLARE `An act` IS ONE OF
    `notify the Insurer of the loss`
    `notify the police or the local authority`
    `notify the Insurer of the theft or disaster loss`
    `move, dismantle or repair the vehicle`
    `pay the indemnity` HAS `the amount` IS A NUMBER
    `explain the refusal`
    `refund the premium` HAS `the amount` IS A NUMBER
    `notify a change in the rating factors`
    `answer the request to reduce the premium`
    `re-assess the risk and the premium`
    `stop processing the personal data`
    `choose the repair shop`

§§ `The supplementary clauses (Decision 17/2022)`

-- (BS01-BS07: their headings and texts are quoted in ocar-17-supplementary.l4, src:1013-1129)
DECLARE `A supplementary clause` IS ONE OF
    `BS01 no depreciation on new parts and materials`
    `BS02 choice of repair shop`
    `BS03 flood damage`
    `BS04 settlement up to a limit of liability`
    `BS05 loss of parts`
    `BS06 safe journey`
    `BS07 modified, extended or added equipment`

-- A supplementary clause the Policyholder asked for, as the contract records it.
-- `accepted by the Insurer`, `premium paid in full`: Article 17, src:982-984.
-- `premium paid on time`: the Article 12 chapeau asks for both, src:588-590.
-- The four MAYBE figures are what each clause leaves to "the contract": NOTHING where the
-- contract states none (BS03 and BS05 then print their own figures; BS04 and BS06 do not).
DECLARE `A supplementary clause on the policy` HAS
    `clause`                             IS A `A supplementary clause`
    `accepted by the Insurer`            IS A BOOLEAN
    `premium paid in full`               IS A BOOLEAN
    `premium paid on time`               IS A BOOLEAN
    `sub-limit in the contract`          IS A MAYBE NUMBER   -- BS04, src:1074-1076
    `benefit limit in the contract`      IS A MAYBE NUMBER   -- BS06, src:1111-1112
    `deductible otherwise agreed`        IS A MAYBE NUMBER   -- BS03 src:1056-1057, BS05 src:1102-1103
    `number of losses otherwise agreed`  IS A MAYBE NUMBER   -- BS05, src:1098-1099

§§ `The vehicle`

-- 1.1: a road vehicle with four or more wheels, not running on rails, not a two- or
-- three-wheeled motorcycle or similar. The listed kinds (car, pickup, truck, coach ...) are
-- examples; `number of wheels` and the two flags are what the definition turns on.
-- (src:64-70, quoted in ocar-01-definitions.l4)
--
-- `origin`: 13.2(i) values a used vehicle "sản xuất trong nước", 13.2(ii) one "nhập khẩu
-- đã qua sử dụng"; 1.15 counts the age of an imported vehicle "đã qua sử dụng ở nước ngoài"
-- from January of its year of manufacture.
DECLARE `The origin of the vehicle` IS ONE OF
    `manufactured in Vietnam`
    `imported new`
    `imported after use abroad`

-- 14.1.2(b): the uses for which depreciation is 150% of the ordinary rate.
-- (src:803-805, quoted in ocar-14-settlement.l4)
DECLARE `A use that raises depreciation` IS ONE OF
    `none of the uses listed in 14.1.2(b)`
    `a bus`
    `a passenger transport business vehicle on a fixed, intra-provincial or inter-provincial route`
    `a self-drive rental vehicle`
    `a taxi`

-- 12.18: goods vehicles are measured by load, passenger vehicles by persons, mixed by either.
-- (src:686-688, quoted in ocar-11-12-cover.l4)
DECLARE `What the vehicle carries` IS ONE OF
    `goods`
    `passengers`
    `goods and passengers`

DECLARE `The vehicle` HAS
    `number of wheels`                                          IS A NUMBER
    `runs on rails`                                             IS A BOOLEAN
    `a two- or three-wheeled motorcycle or a similar vehicle`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `origin`                                                    IS A `The origin of the vehicle`
    `new (100%) when insured`                                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `date of first registration in Vietnam`                     IS A DATE
    `year of manufacture`                                       IS A NUMBER
    `use`                                                       IS A `A use that raises depreciation`
    `carries`                                                   IS A `What the vehicle carries`
    `permitted load in the inspection certificate`              IS A NUMBER
    `permitted number of persons in the inspection certificate` IS A NUMBER

§§ `Another policy on the same vehicle (Article 9)`

-- (src:503-505, quoted in ocar-07-10-claims-process.l4)
DECLARE `Another policy on the vehicle` HAS
    `issued by another insurer`                                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `sum insured`                                               IS A NUMBER
    `same subject, same conditions and same insured event`      IS A BOOLEAN
    `in force at the time of the loss`                          IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `The policy: what the certificate and the contract record`

-- Everything the rules leave to "Hợp Đồng Bảo Hiểm/Giấy Chứng Nhận Bảo Hiểm" is here, as an
-- input with no default.
-- `date the contract was concluded`: 1.15 measures the vehicle's age to "tháng giao kết Hợp
--   Đồng Bảo Hiểm"; this encoding also selects the version of the rules on it (NOTES.md F1).
-- (src:126-129, quoted in ocar-01-definitions.l4)
-- `start` and `last day of the insurance period`: 2.1. The last day is the last day covered.
-- (src:135-136, quoted in ocar-02-03-term-termination.l4)
-- `sum insured`: 1.10.
-- (src:96-98, quoted in ocar-01-definitions.l4)
-- `market value when insured`: 1.9 and 13.1. NOTHING where the parties could not determine
--   it, which is the case 13.2 provides for.
-- (src:736-738, quoted in ocar-13-valuation.l4)
-- `price of the vehicle new (100%)` and `minimum remaining-quality rate in the import customs
--   declaration`: the two figures 13.2 multiplies.
-- `deductible stated in the contract`: 15.2. NOTHING where the contract states none.
-- (src:897-900, quoted in ocar-15-16-deductible-reductions.l4)
-- `reduction level stated in the contract`: the 16.1 chapeau lets the contract state one.
-- (src:913-915, quoted in ocar-15-16-deductible-reductions.l4)
-- `premium`, `premium paid`, `last day for paying the premium`, `the Insurer agreed that the
--   premium may be owed`: 1.7, 2.2 and 3.1.1.
-- (src:162-166, quoted in ocar-02-03-term-termination.l4)
-- `the personal data clause is part of the contract`: the clause on the last pages is not
--   dated (NOTES.md F3); whether it was issued with this contract is on the contract.
-- `the data subject agreed to the whole personal data clause`: its clause 9 (src:1237-1241).
DECLARE `The policy` HAS
    `vehicle`                                                         IS A `The vehicle`
    `date the contract was concluded`                                 IS A DATE
    `start of the insurance period`                                   IS A DATE
    `last day of the insurance period`                                IS A DATE
    `sum insured`                                                     IS A NUMBER
    `market value when insured`                                       IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `price of the vehicle new (100%)`                                 IS A NUMBER
    `minimum remaining-quality rate in the import customs declaration` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `deductible stated in the contract`                               IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `reduction level stated in the contract`                          IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `premium`                                                         IS A NUMBER
    `premium paid`                                                    IS A NUMBER
    `last day for paying the premium`                                 IS A DATE
    `the Insurer agreed that the premium may be owed`                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `supplementary clauses`                                           IS A LIST OF `A supplementary clause on the policy`
    `other policies on the vehicle`                                   IS A LIST OF `Another policy on the vehicle`
    `the personal data clause is part of the contract`                IS A BOOLEAN
    `the data subject agreed to the whole personal data clause`       IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `The loss: what happened`

-- 11.1: the perils, one constructor per word of the five bullets, and two the
-- supplementary clauses add (BS03, BS05), and the residual.
-- (src:566-574, quoted in ocar-11-12-cover.l4)
DECLARE `A peril` IS ONE OF
    `collision or impact, including with another object`   -- Đâm, va
    `overturning`                                           -- lật
    `tipping over`                                          -- đổ
    `sinking`                                               -- chìm
    `the whole vehicle falling`                             -- rơi toàn bộ xe
    `being struck by a falling object`                      -- bị các vật thể khác rơi vào
    `conflagration, fire or explosion`                      -- Hỏa hoạn, cháy, nổ
    `a natural catastrophe`                                 -- tai họa bất khả kháng do thiên nhiên
    `theft or robbery of the whole vehicle`                 -- Mất toàn bộ ... do trộm, cướp
    `a malicious act or deliberate destruction`             -- Hành động ác ý, cố tình phá hoại
    `driving into flood water`                              -- BS03, src:1051-1053
    `theft or robbery of parts`                             -- BS05, src:1082-1085
    `some other cause`

-- 12.3: the driving licence, as the police or the licence itself shows.
-- (src:616-621, quoted in ocar-11-12-cover.l4)
DECLARE `The driving licence` IS ONE OF
    `a valid licence appropriate to the vehicle`
    `no licence`
    `a licence that is invalid or not appropriate to the vehicle`
    `a licence withdrawn, lost, or held by the police past the appointment`

-- 12.2: the state of the inspection certificate (đăng kiểm) when the loss happened.
-- (src:596-605, quoted in ocar-11-12-cover.l4)
DECLARE `The inspection certificate` IS ONE OF
    `valid and in force`
    `missing, invalid, expired or not conforming`
    `lapsed only because tyres or rims were changed within the maker's specification`
    `lapsed only because protective fittings, a roof rack, a winch or a tow hook were added`
    `lapsed only because seats were added`

-- The facts of the event that the exclusions of Article 12 turn on. One field per limb; each
-- is something a police record, an assessment report or a witness establishes.
DECLARE `The circumstances of the loss` HAS
    `deliberately caused by the Policyholder, the Owner, the Driver or a person with an interest in the vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN  -- 12.1
    `the malicious act was by the Policyholder, the Insured, the Owner, the Driver or a person with an interest in the vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN  -- 11.1 bullet 5
    `in traffic`                                                  IS A BOOLEAN                       -- 12.2, 12.3
    `inspection certificate`                                      IS A `The inspection certificate`  -- 12.2
    `driving licence`                                             IS A `The driving licence`         -- 12.3
    `a licence is required for this type of vehicle`              IS A BOOLEAN                       -- 12.3
    `the Driver was over the legal alcohol limit`                 IS A BOOLEAN                       -- 12.4
    `the Driver had used drugs or prohibited stimulants`          IS A BOOLEAN                       -- 12.4
    `a prohibited manoeuvre listed in 12.5`                       IS A BOOLEAN                       -- 12.5
    `stopped or parked where prohibited, leading to the damage`   IS A BOOLEAN                       -- 12.6
    `used for driving practice`                                   IS A BOOLEAN                       -- 12.7
    `driving practice was agreed`                                 IS A BOOLEAN                       -- 12.7
    `used for racing`                                             IS A BOOLEAN                       -- 12.7
    `towing another vehicle unlawfully`                           IS A BOOLEAN                       -- 12.7
    `carrying goods unlawfully or without the loading safety rules` IS A BOOLEAN                     -- 12.8
    `in Vietnam`                                                  IS A BOOLEAN                       -- 12.9
    `war, terrorism, civil war, strike or riot`                   IS A BOOLEAN                       -- 12.10
    `total loss by fraud or abuse of trust`                       IS A BOOLEAN                       -- 12.16
    `caused by the vehicle's own special-purpose equipment`       IS A BOOLEAN                       -- 12.17
    `claim information proven by the Insurer untruthful or forged` IS A BOOLEAN                      -- 12.22
    `important information omitted`                               IS A BOOLEAN                      -- 12.22
    `the omission was inadvertent`                                IS A BOOLEAN                      -- 12.22
    `overhauled, modified or converted and not yet re-inspected`   IS A BOOLEAN                      -- 12.24

-- 12.18, 12.21, 16.1.2 and 16.1.5 measure against the inspection certificate and a speed
-- limit. `speed above the limit` is the excess as a share of the limit (0.3 for 30% over),
-- as an authority's written conclusion finds it; NOTHING where there is no such conclusion.
-- `persons carried, not counting children under 7`: 12.18 does not count them; 16.1.5 does
-- not say so, hence the two counts (NOTES.md, finding X4).
-- (src:683-685, quoted in ocar-11-12-cover.l4)
DECLARE `The load and speed` HAS
    `load carried`                                     IS A NUMBER
    `persons carried, counting children under 7`       IS A NUMBER
    `persons carried, not counting children under 7`   IS A NUMBER
    `speed above the limit, by an authority's written conclusion` IS A MAYBE NUMBER

-- The facts of conduct that Article 16 reduces the indemnity for. Each limb of 16.1.1 to
-- 16.1.6 is a field; each is a fact, not a finding that the reduction applies.
-- `date the Insurer was notified of the loss`: NOTHING where it never was.
DECLARE `The conduct after the loss` HAS
    `date the Insurer was notified of the loss`                       IS A MAYBE DATE           -- 5.2, 16.1.1
    `force majeure prevented notice`                                  IS A BOOLEAN              -- 5.2, 16.1.1
    `the Insurer assessed the damage within those 5 days`             IS A BOOLEAN              -- 16.1.1
    `the hotline was told at the time of the accident`                IS A BOOLEAN              -- 16.1.1
    `rescue and mitigation measures were not fully taken`             IS A BOOLEAN              -- 16.1.1
    `the police or local authority were not told at once`             IS A BOOLEAN              -- 16.1.1, 5.2
    `the Insurer was not told at once`                                IS A BOOLEAN              -- 16.1.1, 5.2
    `the Insurer's instructions were not followed`                    IS A BOOLEAN              -- 16.1.1
    `parked on a slope without brakes or chocks, so it rolled`        IS A BOOLEAN              -- 16.1.1
    `dismantled or repaired without the Insurer's approval`           IS A BOOLEAN              -- 16.1.3
    `the Insurer gave no opinion within 5 working days of the notice` IS A BOOLEAN              -- 5.2, 16.1.3
    `the scene was not protected or the vehicle was moved from it`    IS A BOOLEAN              -- 16.1.4
    `it was necessary for safety, to limit loss, or on an authority's order` IS A BOOLEAN       -- 16.1.3, 16.1.4
    `the Owner did not preserve and transfer the claim against the third party` IS A BOOLEAN    -- 16.1.4
    `the Owner was untruthful in the claim documents`                 IS A BOOLEAN              -- 16.1.4
    `the use of the vehicle was misdeclared, so less premium was charged` IS A BOOLEAN          -- 16.1.6
    `an increase in risk was not notified`                            IS A BOOLEAN              -- 16.1.6
    `premium that should have been paid`                              IS A NUMBER               -- 16.1.6

-- One part or item of the vehicle that was damaged or lost. The kinds are those Articles 12
-- and 14 and the supplementary clauses name; `an ordinary part` is every other part.
-- (src:667-671, quoted in ocar-11-12-cover.l4; src:828-839 in ocar-14-settlement.l4)
DECLARE `A kind of part` IS ONE OF
    `an ordinary part`
    `glass or a mirror`                     -- kính, mặt gương (14.1.2(d) note)
    `air-conditioning gas`                  -- gas của hệ thống điều hòa nhiệt độ
    `coolant`                               -- nước mát
    `lubricating oil`                       -- dầu bôi trơn
    `a battery`                             -- ắc quy
    `a truck-bed canvas`                    -- bạt thùng xe
    `a tyre or an inner tube`               -- săm, lốp
    `a label or a sticker`                  -- tem chữ, nhãn mác, tem nhãn mác
    `the maker's emblem`                    -- biểu tượng của nhà sản xuất (12.14)
    `a hubcap`                              -- ốp chụp la-zăng (12.14)
    `a key or a remote`                     -- chìa khóa cơ/chìa khóa điện/điều khiển điện
    `an underbody shield`                   -- tấm lót gầm (12.14)
    `a periodically replaced consumable`    -- gioăng, phớt, lọc gió, lọc dầu, lọc xăng, vòng bi (BS01)
    `added protective equipment`            -- hệ thống báo động, bảo vệ cản trước, bảo vệ cản sau (12.19)
    `other added equipment or accessory`    -- thiết bị/phụ kiện lắp thêm (12.19, BS07)

-- How the assessment settles the item (14.1.1(a), 14.1.2(b) last paragraph, 14.1.3).
DECLARE `How the item is put right` IS ONE OF
    `repaired`
    `replaced with a new part`
    `replaced with an equivalent used part, as the shop, the Policyholder and the Insurer agreed`

DECLARE `A damaged item` HAS
    `kind`                                                     IS A `A kind of part`
    `put right by`                                             IS A `How the item is put right`
    `can be repaired`                                          IS A BOOLEAN   -- 14.1.3
    `reasonable cost of repair`                                IS A NUMBER    -- 14.1.1(a), 14.1.3
    `cost of a new replacement`                                IS A NUMBER    -- 14.1.2(b), 14.1.3
    `cost of the used replacement part`                        IS A NUMBER    -- 14.1.2(b) last paragraph
    `lost`                                                     IS A BOOLEAN   -- 12.15, BS05
    `damaged or lost by the same cause and at the same time as other parts in the same accident` IS A BOOLEAN  -- 12.14, 12.15
    `wear and tear, inherent nature, defect, or damage in repair` IS A BOOLEAN  -- 12.11, first sentence
    `an indirect loss: lower commercial value, or loss tied to using the vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN  -- 12.11, second sentence
    `a consequential loss, as 12.23 defines it`                IS A BOOLEAN   -- 12.23
    `engine damage from water: flood water or hydrolock`       IS A BOOLEAN   -- 12.12
    `water entered after an accidental plunge into a pond, lake, river or stream` IS A BOOLEAN  -- 12.12
    `electrical or mechanical breakdown not caused by an insured peril` IS A BOOLEAN  -- 12.13
    `electrical damage from overload, overpressure, short circuit, self-heating, arcing or leakage` IS A BOOLEAN  -- 12.13
    `the loss was caused by the added equipment or the modification` IS A BOOLEAN  -- 12.19
    `approved by the registry and within the inspection's validity` IS A BOOLEAN  -- BS07 (i)
    `depreciation rate agreed at the assessment`                IS A MAYBE NUMBER  -- 14.1.2(d), tyres, tubes, labels

-- What the assessment and the investigation established about the loss as a whole.
-- `assessed damage` and `assessed cost of repair` are the two measures 14.2.1 compares with
-- 75% of the market value immediately before the loss.
DECLARE `The loss` HAS
    `date of the loss`                                          IS A DATE
    `peril`                                                     IS A `A peril`
    `sudden and unforeseeable`                                  IS A BOOLEAN   -- 11.1 chapeau
    `circumstances`                                             IS A `The circumstances of the loss`
    `load and speed`                                            IS A `The load and speed`
    `conduct`                                                   IS A `The conduct after the loss`
    `items`                                                     IS A LIST OF `A damaged item`
    `share of the painted area damaged`                         IS A NUMBER    -- 14.1.4
    `cost of repainting the damaged panels`                     IS A NUMBER    -- 14.1.4
    `cost of repainting the whole vehicle`                      IS A NUMBER    -- 14.1.4
    `cost of protecting the scene and preventing further loss`  IS A NUMBER    -- 11.2
    `cost of rescue and transport to the nearest repair shop`   IS A NUMBER    -- 11.2
    `the costs were incurred at the Insurer's request and direction` IS A BOOLEAN  -- 11.2
    `market value immediately before the loss`                  IS A NUMBER    -- 14.2.1, 14.2.3
    `assessed damage`                                           IS A NUMBER    -- 14.2.1
    `assessed cost of repair`                                   IS A NUMBER    -- 14.2.1
    `a court judgment, or a decision to suspend the investigation or not to prosecute` IS A BOOLEAN  -- 14.2.2
    `the Owner asks to keep the wreck`                          IS A BOOLEAN   -- 14.3.2
    `value of the wreck, as valued`                             IS A NUMBER    -- 14.3.2

§§ `The claim file (Article 8)`

-- The documents Article 8 lists, one member per bullet (the seven items of the police file in
-- 8.2 are one member, as the bullet that introduces them is one).
DECLARE `A claim document` IS ONE OF
    `notice of the accident and claim, on the Insurer's form`                          -- 8.1
    `the certificate or the contract, and other written agreements`                    -- 8.1
    `the vehicle registration, and the Driver's licence valid at the time of the loss` -- 8.1
    `papers on a sale, transfer, gift or authorised use of the vehicle`                -- 8.1, if any
    `a valid inspection certificate, or an equivalent paper`                           -- 8.1
    `invoices for towing`                                                              -- 8.1, if any
    `invoices for repair or replacement outside the Insurer's guarantee network`       -- 8.1
    `papers fixing the value of the property`                                          -- 8.1, if needed
    `an authority's record of the theft or disappearance of the vehicle`               -- 8.1
    `papers proving the costs of limiting the loss or following the Insurer's instructions` -- 8.1
    `the record of a settlement or mediation`                                          -- 8.1
    `a court judgment or decision in force`                                            -- 8.1, if any
    `papers transferring the claim against the third party to the Insurer`             -- 8.1
    `copies of the police file on the accident`                                        -- 8.2
    `papers on the liability of a third party`                                         -- 8.2, if any
    `the assessment report the parties agreed`                                         -- 8.2
    `other relevant papers`                                                            -- 8.2, if any
    `the theft or robbery report, confirmed by the police`                             -- 8.3
    `the decision to prosecute and investigate`                                        -- 8.3, if any
    `the decision to suspend the investigation or the prosecution`                     -- 8.3, if any
    `a police-confirmed declaration of papers lost with the vehicle`                   -- 8.3, if any

-- The facts on which Article 8 makes a document part of the file: each "nếu có" (if any) or
-- "trong trường hợp" (in the case of) in the list is one of these.
DECLARE `The facts the claim file depends on` HAS
    `the vehicle was sold, transferred, given or lent under an authority` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the vehicle runs under a temporary permit or is in its first registration` IS A BOOLEAN
    `towing was hired`                                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `repaired outside the Insurer's guarantee network`       IS A BOOLEAN
    `a valuation is needed`                                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the whole vehicle was stolen, robbed or disappeared`    IS A BOOLEAN
    `costs were incurred to limit the loss or on the Insurer's instructions` IS A BOOLEAN
    `there was a mediation`                                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `there is a court judgment or decision`                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `a third party is liable`                                IS A BOOLEAN
    `the police dealt with the accident`                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `there are other relevant papers`                        IS A BOOLEAN
    `there is a decision to prosecute`                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `there is a decision to suspend`                         IS A BOOLEAN
    `papers were lost with the vehicle`                      IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `The claim`

-- What was already paid in the same insurance period: BS04 caps its own settlements by a
-- sub-limit "in the period" (src:1070-1071), BS05 counts the number of parts losses
-- (src:1097-1099). Records of the Insurer's own payments.
DECLARE `The earlier claims in the period` HAS
    `indemnity already paid under BS04 in the period`    IS A NUMBER
    `parts losses already paid under BS05 in the period` IS A NUMBER

-- BS06: the facts of the journey after an accident.
-- (src:1108-1115, quoted in ocar-17-supplementary.l4)
DECLARE `The safe-journey costs` HAS
    `the vehicle could not move or be driven safely`                                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `cost of overnight stay and transport to the destination for the driver and occupants` IS A NUMBER
    `valid financial invoices were supplied`                                               IS A BOOLEAN

-- One claim: the policy, the loss, and what the claim depends on from outside the loss.
DECLARE `The claim` HAS
    `policy`             IS A `The policy`
    `loss`               IS A `The loss`
    `earlier claims`     IS A `The earlier claims in the period`
    `safe-journey costs` IS A `The safe-journey costs`

§§ `The version of the rules`

-- The heading names two instruments: the rules issued by Decision 124/2019 of 31/12/2019,
-- and the supplementary clauses issued by Decision 17/2022 of 28/03/2022 that amend them.
-- (src:5-7, quoted in ocar-01-definitions.l4)
DECLARE `The version of the rules` IS ONE OF
    `the rules as made by Decision 124/2019`
    `the rules as amended by the supplementary clauses of Decision 17/2022`

§§ `The exclusions of Article 12`

-- The answer type of "which exclusions apply": one member per clause of Article 12.
DECLARE `An exclusion in Article 12` IS ONE OF
    `12.1 deliberate act`
    `12.2 no valid inspection certificate`
    `12.3 no valid driving licence`
    `12.4 alcohol or drugs`
    `12.5 prohibited manoeuvre`
    `12.6 prohibited stopping or parking`
    `12.7 driving practice, racing or unlawful towing`
    `12.8 unlawful or unsafe carriage of goods`
    `12.9 outside Vietnam`
    `12.10 war, terrorism, strike or riot`
    `12.11 wear, defects and indirect loss`
    `12.12 water damage to the engine`
    `12.13 electrical or mechanical breakdown`
    `12.14 tyres, canvas, emblems, keys and the like`
    `12.15 loss of parts`
    `12.16 fraud or abuse of trust`
    `12.17 the vehicle's own special-purpose equipment`
    `12.18 overloading by 50% or more`
    `12.19 added equipment`
    `12.20 at or below the deductible`
    `12.21 speeding by more than 50%`
    `12.22 untruthful or forged claim information`
    `12.23 consequential loss`
    `12.24 overhaul or conversion not re-inspected`

§§ `The reductions of Article 16`

-- The answer type of "which reductions may the Insurer make": one member per limb of 16.1.
DECLARE `A ground of reduction in Article 16` IS ONE OF
    `16.1.1 notice of the loss not sent within 5 days`
    `16.1.1 mitigation, reporting or instructions not followed`
    `16.1.1 parked on a slope without brakes or chocks`
    `16.1.2 speeding by 20% to 50%`
    `16.1.3 dismantled or repaired without approval`
    `16.1.4 scene not protected or vehicle moved`
    `16.1.4 claim against the third party not preserved or transferred`
    `16.1.4 untruthful claim documents`
    `16.1.5 overloading by over 20% and under 50%`
    `16.1.6 use misdeclared`
    `16.1.6 increase in risk not notified`

-- A reduction the Insurer may make, as a range of rates of the indemnity; 16.1.5 and 16.1.6
-- fix the rate, so their lowest and highest rates are equal.
DECLARE `A reduction the Insurer may make` HAS
    `ground`       IS A `A ground of reduction in Article 16`
    `lowest rate`  IS A NUMBER
    `highest rate` IS A NUMBER

§§ `A problem with the facts`

-- Invalid input is rejected, not answered: the caller can fix it.
DECLARE `A problem with the facts` IS ONE OF
    `the reduction rate is not one Article 16 allows`
